WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:00.923
- Hey guys.

00:00:00.923 --> 00:00:03.860
I'm no master chef, but I'm
in a rush in my daily life,

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:06.450
so I need quick, healthy,
easy meal options

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:07.510
to make during the day.

00:00:07.510 --> 00:00:08.630
So let's get some ingredients.

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:10.520
I got my new school
shopping list right here.

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:11.986
No more pen and paper.

00:00:11.986 --> 00:00:14.569
(upbeat music)

00:00:39.424 --> 00:00:42.018
(grocery bags rustling)

00:00:42.018 --> 00:00:43.068
(door slamming shut)

00:00:43.068 --> 00:00:43.901
(grocery bags rustling)

00:00:43.901 --> 00:00:46.330
I'm no Gordon Ramsay when it
comes to being in the kitchen,

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:48.640
but I do know a thing
or two about nutrition.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:52.080
These are five quick,
easy, and nutritious meals

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:54.620
that you can make at home
when you're on the go.

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:57.563
Enter Chef Dr. Mik.

00:00:59.207 --> 00:01:01.522
(upbeat music)

00:01:01.522 --> 00:01:02.355
(hitting sound effect)

00:01:02.355 --> 00:01:03.313
(bell dinging)

00:01:03.313 --> 00:01:05.896
(upbeat music)

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:11.270
Let's start with my favorite dish.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:14.580
I like to call this bad boy The Underdog,

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:17.570
'cause most people think sardines, ew, no.

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:19.710
First of all, sardines are delicious.

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:21.510
Second of all, they're an excellent source

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:23.490
of omega 3 fatty acids.

00:01:23.490 --> 00:01:24.640
That's the stuff that you need

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:27.340
to develop a healthy brain, healthy eyes.

00:01:27.340 --> 00:01:28.710
We've seen a lot of studies show

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:31.630
that people who consume
fish on a regular basis

00:01:31.630 --> 00:01:34.100
not only are smarter, but
they also sleep better.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:38.370
Below that, you have guacamole
that has hass avocados in it.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:41.700
It has tomatoes, it has
onions, rich in vegetables.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:44.270
All on tip of this crisp bread

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:46.680
which has sunflower seeds, flax seeds,

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:49.370
sesame seeds, it's rich in whole grains,

00:01:49.370 --> 00:01:52.300
has three grams of fiber,
three grams of protein.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:55.200
This is a killer nutritious snack

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:56.830
that you can really eat on the go.

00:01:56.830 --> 00:01:58.567
Don't mind a sardine.

00:01:58.567 --> 00:02:00.588
(upbeat music)

00:02:00.588 --> 00:02:01.421
(hitting sound effect)

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:02.576
(bell dinging)

00:02:02.576 --> 00:02:05.159
(upbeat music)

00:02:08.340 --> 00:02:10.820
Up next we have something
that I munched on

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:12.260
all the time in college.

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:13.930
The Dorm Room Special.

00:02:13.930 --> 00:02:15.150
It's really simple.

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:16.430
It's not elegant.

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:17.800
But it really does the trick.

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:21.220
Oven roasted turkey breast
followed by my favorite cheese,

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:24.610
muenster cheese, and then you
have two slices of cucumbers.

00:02:24.610 --> 00:02:27.250
A lot of nutrition packed
into this little bad boy here.

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:29.600
You have proteins from
the cheese and the turkey

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:31.720
and then you have antioxidants

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:33.920
and polyphenols from the cucumbers.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.590
Cucumbers contain lichenins
and they have a strong

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:38.140
history of research in connection

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:40.880
with reduced risk of
cardiovascular disease

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:42.520
as well as some cancers even.

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:45.243
And who doesn't like themselves
a little extra crunch?

00:02:47.101 --> 00:02:48.438
(Mikhail popping mouth)

00:02:48.438 --> 00:02:50.266
(upbeat music)

00:02:50.266 --> 00:02:51.113
(hitting sound effect)

00:02:51.113 --> 00:02:51.946
(bell dinging)

00:02:51.946 --> 00:02:54.529
(upbeat music)

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:01.150
The Antioxidant 1-2 Punch.

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:02.090
That's right.

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:05.130
The reason why I call
this Antioxidant 1-2 Punch

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:08.210
is because green apples,
my favorite kind of apples,

00:03:08.210 --> 00:03:11.750
yes, Granny Smith, have
a ton of antioxidants

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:14.670
as well as polyphenols, so the saying

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:17.450
an apple a day keeps your
doctor away is partially true,

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:20.400
because they do have a
host of health benefits.

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:23.910
They also are rich in fiber
which keeps you fuller longer.

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:26.290
It also helps with sugar management.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:29.700
Then you have on the side
as a little dipping portion

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:34.700
of cottage cheese, rich
in protein, calcium, B12,

00:03:34.870 --> 00:03:37.650
all essential nutrients
to keep your body going.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.900
And you finally top it off with
a little bit of extra flavor

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:43.450
from cinnamon, which is zero calories.

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:46.050
That's right, zero calories.

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:48.870
And cinnamon also loaded in antioxidants.

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:51.040
That's the two in the 1-2 Punch.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:52.730
Cinnamon has shown promise in

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:54.560
preventing issues with your heart.

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:57.360
It's also shown to help
better manage sugar

00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:00.160
within your body, whether
you're diabetic of not diabetic.

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:04.559
Antioxidant 1-2 Punch tastes
great and low calorie.

00:04:04.559 --> 00:04:06.310
(upbeat music)

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:07.228
(hitting sound effect)

00:04:07.228 --> 00:04:08.061
(bell dinging)

00:04:08.061 --> 00:04:10.728
(upbeat music)

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:16.260
The Bear Pleaser.

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:18.760
Yup, I named this after my puppy Bear.

00:04:18.760 --> 00:04:22.330
And what this is is
just basic Greek yogurt

00:04:22.330 --> 00:04:25.860
mixed with some multigrain,
gluten free granola.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:27.650
I added a couple walnuts for myself,

00:04:27.650 --> 00:04:30.070
because I love walnuts,
and then finish off

00:04:30.070 --> 00:04:31.410
with a little drizzle of honey.

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:33.690
Greek yogurt, rich in protein

00:04:33.690 --> 00:04:36.390
and a great source of probiotics.

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:38.820
Yeah, probiotics is all
that bacteria that lives

00:04:38.820 --> 00:04:40.780
within inside your gut that helps you

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:43.650
to have healthy digestion,
helps you to go to the bathroom

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:45.730
more regularly, normal stools.

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:48.060
We've seen a lot of benefits
from people eating yogurt.

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:50.120
The multigrain granola is great,

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:51.960
because the one I buy has actually

00:04:51.960 --> 00:04:54.690
nine different seeds and nuts in it.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:55.860
You're getting a lot of of fiber.

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:57.980
You're getting a lot
of nutrients packed in

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:00.130
and that crunch is unbelievable.

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:01.810
I think that yogurt on its own,

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:03.878
especially plain yogurt and granola,

00:05:03.878 --> 00:05:05.510
is kind of tasteless.

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:07.720
So what I do is I take my favorite,

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:09.710
I guess food topping you could call it,

00:05:09.710 --> 00:05:11.910
and I drizzle a little
bit of honey on top,

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.400
give it a ton of flavor,

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:15.420
because honey is rich in sugar.

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:18.220
But honey is also rich in polyphenols,

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:21.340
antioxidants, and we've
seen some promising studies

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:24.110
talking about the favorable
effect on cholesterol.

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:27.702
So this is a meal that
I love and Bear loves.

00:05:27.702 --> 00:05:30.285
(upbeat music)

00:05:33.011 --> 00:05:33.844
(hitting sound effect)

00:05:33.844 --> 00:05:34.677
(bell dinging)

00:05:34.677 --> 00:05:37.260
(upbeat music)

00:05:40.720 --> 00:05:43.300
Last and least.

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:46.140
It may not be the most
adult one of these five,

00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:49.560
but it's certainly a favorite
of mine in childhood.

00:05:49.560 --> 00:05:50.910
Peanut butter and jelly.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:52.560
Peanut butter really gets a bad rap

00:05:52.560 --> 00:05:54.470
because it's high in fat.

00:05:54.470 --> 00:05:57.600
It has some saturated
fats and in small amounts

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:59.400
saturated fats are not bad for you.

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:01.360
And it's rich in unsaturated fats

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:02.570
which are also good for you.

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:04.900
Peanut butter is also a great way

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:07.280
for people who are vegetarian or vegan

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:08.520
to get their protein up.

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:10.550
When selecting the bread for your PB &amp; J,

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:13.380
make sure it's one that has
whole grain and whole wheat

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:15.650
in the first two ingredients to make sure

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:17.640
it's the healthiest type
of bread that you can get.

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:18.670
Rich in fiber.

00:06:18.670 --> 00:06:20.130
If you're gonna choose a jam,

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:21.820
make sure it's a high quality jam,

00:06:21.820 --> 00:06:24.740
not just jam that's packed
with a ton of sugar.

00:06:24.740 --> 00:06:26.773
Make sure it's made with real fruit.

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:30.310
Clearly you don't need
to put in a lot of effort

00:06:30.310 --> 00:06:33.310
to make really quick and nutritious foods.

00:06:33.310 --> 00:06:36.120
I mean, most of these here
have three or four ingredients

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:39.030
at most and maybe they took
me five minutes to make.

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:41.819
As always guys, stay happy and healthy.

